  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origin and Core Doctrine
    
    Pactum∴myster arose during the Clever Ice Age in the thermal vent warrens near Thrall☽ Vavmastius, a volcanic site deep within Nightfall Shelf. Its first known teacher was Zhachelang zhihi'Opalum — an Aurora Stack merchant, not a Nightshelf native, a detail the doctrine's adherents rarely volunteer. The central claim is theological: that fire-memory and aurora-memory are severed halves of a single divinity, and that communion with both permits contact with something vast stirring beneath the frozen sea. That the doctrine's founder was a surface-dweller teaching in absolute darkness lends the theology a structural coherence its critics have not adequately addressed.
    
    ## Practice and Transmission
    
    Adherents carve ☽'visois' Mask, a ritual artifact, into their own bone-work — a permanent physical binding. The doctrine may not be taught by voice. Transmission occurs solely through the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, a Nightshelf time-fracturing technique here repurposed as liturgy: patterns traced in ash and blood on stone. These spirals sometimes manifest with gaps, sections where the pattern should continue but does not. Whether the gaps represent degradation or deliberate omission is unresolved.
    
    The silence demanded is comprehensive. Adherents who share personal confidences — not doctrine, but ordinary tenderness — report their communion-visions dimming proportionally. Those who break the oath entirely lose contact with the deep. The doctrine is thus self-selecting for isolation. The chronicle of the hermit magister ☽'Naevaeum~, who chose to speak a full sentence to Zhachelang and surrendered their sight for it, suggests the mechanism is indifferent to the speaker's reasons.
    
    ## Institutional Adoption and Present Status
    
    Pactum∴myster has calcified into tradition across the Nightshelf, adopted by ☽'ofund' Guild merchants and The Communion, an elt-sworn cult. It commemorates The Mbra∴silentiu and The Abys∴uina, a catastrophic thermal collapse that killed hundreds. Written grievances filed by believers have reportedly redacted themselves upon being read. The doctrine's prominence has faded; its silence has seen to that.
